        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "force at support.",
            "block_bbox": [
                344,
                267,
                516,
                290
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\begin{aligned}V_{u}=&\\frac{r_{u}L}{2}\\\\ =&\\frac{1.23(150)}{2}=92\\ lb/in\\end{aligned}",
            "block_bbox": [
                347,
                312,
                598,
                427
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C.Check connection strength of dowels matching wall reinforcement acting in shear friction at supports (Equation 6-8). Note that the dynamic increase factor for shear reinforcing steel in Table 6-2 (+)is 1.0.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                286,
                449,
                1031,
                551
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\begin{aligned}&V_{dm}=0.6A_{vd}f_{dy}\\\\ &\\quad=0.6(\\frac{0.2in^2}{16in})(66000)\\\\ &\\quad=495Ib/j\\eta>92Ib/j\\eta\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
            "block_bbox": [
                347,
                576,
                633,
                704
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The direct shear strength of the dowels across the top and bottom support of the wall exceeds the connection design load – OK ",
            "block_bbox": [
                344,
                730,
                1029,
                780
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Step 16.Check the response of the wall as a shear wall resisting the dynamic reaction at the top of the wall on the perpendicular side of the building to blast load. Since the building plan has a 2:1 aspect ratio $(\\mathsf{i.e.}~\\mathsf{L_{2}}/\\mathsf{L_{1}}=2)$ ,the in-plane shear can be calculated as shown below using $\\mathsf{V}_{\\mathsf{u}}$ in Step 15b.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                801,
                1047,
                907
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a.Calculate in-plane shear force for the worst case shear wall.",
            "block_bbox": [
                274,
                927,
                967,
                949
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\begin{aligned}V_{ui}=&\\frac{V_{u}L_{2}}{2L_{1}}\\\\ =&\\frac{(92lb/in)2}{2}\\\\ =&92lb/in\\end{aligned}",
            "block_bbox": [
                348,
                973,
                518,
                1130
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b. Find the in-plane shear area (Equation 6-4b).$K_{v}=0$ for a partially grouted wall. The face shell thickness $t_{s}$ is shown in Table 6-1 (+)",
            "block_bbox": [
                281,
                1157,
                1002,
                1207
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "formula",
            "block_content": "\\begin{aligned}{A_{n i}}&{{}=(K_{v}T+(1-K_{v})2t_{s})\\frac{L_{v}}{L}}\\\\ {}&{{}=(0(7.63)+(1-0)(2)(1.25))0.8}\\\\ {}&{{}=2.0i n^{2}/i n}\\\\ \\end{aligned}",
            "block_bbox": [
                348,
